"Open your Level 2 Data or DOM (Depth of Market): You can access this in your trading platform, such as using the "Active Trader" ladder or "Level II Gadget" in thinkorswim, or the "Market Depth Trader" in IBKR TWS
. This tool shows you a vertical list of all the bids and asks sitting at different price levels, along with exactly how many shares are waiting in line to trade
.
Spot "Liquidity Walls": Look for giant resting orders. For example, if you see a massive wall of limit sell orders stacked up and waiting at $150, you know the stock will likely struggle to break past that price due to the heavy supply
.
Gauge Market Aggression: Technicals show you where a trade should happen, but order flow confirms it is happening
. Watch the tape to see if the market is aggressively "eating through" sell orders on the ask, which signals strong upward momentum and confirms that buyers are willing to pay higher prices
.
Confirm with Relative Volume (RVOL): Look for massive volume spikes compared to previous days to confirm that large institutions are actively participating in the price move"


