[2026-09-01] --- [13:55:36]
Business activities:

Inventory management: Tracking warehouse stock levels using basic formulas, then throwing that data into a pie chart to easily see which products are eating up the most shelf space at a quick glance.

Order fulfillment and deliveries: Using large worksheets to track daily delivery routes and basic formulas to calculate total weekly mileage, then charting the data to visually pinpoint peak delivery times.

Non-business activities:

Household yearly inventory: Applying that exact same business inventory mentality to your house. You can track yearly household supplies and bulk items using basic formulas to calculate annual costs, then chart the data to see exactly which categories are eating up your budget.

Tracking functional strength training: Logging reps, sets, and weights for a given routine, then using line charts to visually track your performance trends and strength progression over the year.

