[2026-09-01] --- [18:04:11]
I use basic functions like 'SUM' and 'AVERAGE' all the time alongside charts. Basic 'IF' statements are another commonly used tool, but nesting If-Then-Else logic is even more fun, and the usefulness of it is so broad.

For the more advanced tools, Goal Seek and Data Tables are incredibly useful for future planning. If I have a specific savings or investment target I want to hit by the end of the year, Goal Seek works backwards to tell me exactly how much I need to put away each month to reach it. Data Tables are great for comparing different what-if scenarios side-by-side, like looking at how a range of different interest rates would change the monthly payment on a potential car loan.

[2026-09-01] --- [18:07:09]
I use basic functions like 'SUM' and 'AVERAGE' all the time alongside charts to easily track things like my monthly budget and expenses. Basic 'IF' statements are another commonly used tool for me, but nesting If-Then-Else logic is even more fun, and the usefulness of it is incredibly broad when dealing with raw data. I usually pair those nested IFs with conditional formatting so that my spreadsheet automatically reacts—like highlighting a cell in red if a specific budget category accidentally exceeds its monthly limit for example.

For the more advanced tools, Goal Seek and Data Tables are incredibly useful for future planning. If I have a specific savings or investment target I want to hit by the end of the year, Goal Seek works backwards to tell me exactly how much I need to put away each month to reach it without any guesswork. Data Tables are great for comparing different what-if scenarios side-by-side, like looking at how a range of different interest rates would change the monthly payment on a potential car loan. Combining all these tools turns a basic spreadsheet into an automated planning assistant.

